From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:46:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Error the body of a fetch() response on any network
 error

`fetch()` errored the body stream of its response only when the body
failed to decode, and closed it for every other network error that ended
the body, so a reader saw a body that ended early as complete. A
`WebAssembly.compileStreaming()` consumer was ended normally even when
the body failed to decode.

Error the body stream with a TypeError whenever the body ends with a
network error, as the fetch response handover does when the stream
errors, and end the WebAssembly consumer with `streamError`. SpiderMonkey
rejects the compilation with the exception the stream error callback leaves
pending, and leaves the promise unsettled without one, so the callback now
throws the TypeError instead of only logging. A stream that is no longer
readable, because it was cancelled, errored by an aborted `fetch()` call,
or already errored with the network error of the response, is left as it
is instead of hitting the assertion in `ReadableStream::error`.

A consumer that refuses a chunk has been ended by SpiderMonkey, which
then deletes it, so it is dropped instead of being fed or ended again.

Net still ends a body cut short by the connection as complete; that
changes in a later patch, so the cut-short case of the new test is
expected to fail until then.

Validation: `./mach check` passes. New test `tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/mozilla/wasm-streaming-network-error.any.js` (window and dedicated worker): its decode error cases pass; its cut-short cases are expected to fail until `net: End a body cut short by the connection with a network error`, and pass with it. A focused WPT run of `fetch/api`, `fetch/content-*`, `wasm/webapi`, `xhr`, `eventsource`, `navigation-timing` and the `link`/`style` element tests with this and the next four patches has no unexpected results in the upstream tests except `wasm/webapi/historical.any.js`, which times out in whichever variant runs after another and does the same on the previous patch.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote this patch and its test following docs/fetch-p4a-truncated-body-audit-2026-10-22.md in the workspace, and applied an independent review's findings)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
